From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:38:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test(sim): pin the carried corner sliver of an outside
 contour as true rest

The 50 x 50 part in 60 x 60 stock, contoured with EM-0600-4FL (a 6 mm
end mill, not 0.6 in), leaves full-height slivers at the stock corners
because the round-cornered offset sweeps only 6 mm from each part corner
and the stock corner is 7.07 mm away. The carried body matches that
geometry column by column; with an 8 mm tool it keeps no corner material.
No sim or carry change.

Fixes #1551

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
